    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656-a1">

                <pb facs="1059" n="963" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg963"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    886.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. José de Carvajal to General Sickles.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of State, Private Cabinet</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-11-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 26, 1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Private.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General</hi>: A common friend has given me to
                    understand that the note I sent you this morning at an early hour had not
                    reached your hands when at 2 o’clock in the afternoon you sent me yours asking
                    your passports, and that it would be agreeable to you if action were not taken
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">no se diera cur so</hi>) on the latter.</p>
                <p>For my part, I can assure you that this would also be very satisfactory to me,
                    and I beg that you will kindly let me know if I may do so, thus accomplishing
                    the desires of both.</p>
                <p>I repeat, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">De</hi> CARVAJAL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
